  "attribution": {
    "42504417": "Number 6 plate and matching close crop 42504416; red upper canopy, upper open rail and enclosed lower glazed front, timber screen over courtyard wall. At image left see part of adjoining green-framed enclosure.",
    "42504418": "Plate 7 at (98,424) on left gate pier with right pier around (214,427). Gate center is not the center of the green enclosure. Glazed left half and open right half of two levels adjoin the red 6 canopy at right. The leftmost pair of sash windows is captured again in 19 and is not assigned to the enclosure.",
    "42504419": "Author labels only the lane. Continuous with 7 via the paired metal windows and with the 9 shot via the open balcony. This infers the intermediate stretch of the row; no unambiguous plate identifies the individual yellow window bay.",
    "42504420": "Number 9 caption & plate on left pier at (122,388). Opposite end of yard wall near (611,381) also has a green plate, about 10 pixels wide in the 500px source: unresolved digit. Twin open slab-and-bar terraces, a central divider/drain, and the adjoining enclosed yellow bay at right."
  },
  "source_scope": "500x375 legacy original source URLs and 650x487 CDN derivatives carry the same photos. EXIF dimensions remain 500x375, so the 650 images add no established original optical detail. The maker GPS namespace contains only version, not geolocation. Writer says three storeys; courtyard walls screen much of ground storey. Blue/green hue and pale render are observed appearance, not original color specification. The Gao oblique utility wall is unpaired: no architectural tie to this courtyard set. No photo pixels are cleared for redistribution.",
